# Project inbox — external material staged for triage (LIFECYCLE.md).
# An item is either filed (and the FILED artefact is what gets committed)
# or discarded; committing staging would preserve exactly what triage
# exists to resolve.
#
# ANCHORED. Unanchored `inbox/` matches a directory of that name at ANY
# depth, so it also ignored `docs/features/inbox/` — FEAT-0045, its PLAN and
# TASK-0232/0233/0234 were never in the repository, and a fresh clone failed
# validate-docs.py because SNAPSHOT metrics counted notes the clone could not
# see. Found by independent review, 2026-07-30 (ISS-0070). Only the staging
# directory at the repo root is meant here.
/inbox/
